  "kanji": "暮",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 暮\ntitle: dusk; livelihood\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-6, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 14\nradical: 日\nradicalNumber: 72\nonyomi: [ボ]\nkunyomi: [く.れる, く.らす]\ndistractors: [春, 映, 早]\n---\n\n# 暮 — dusk; livelihood\n\n**Strokes:** 14 · **Key (radical):** 日 (no. 72) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n暮 has two useful word families. 暮れる くれる describes daylight fading or a period coming to an end;\n[暮らす](../words/暮らす.md) くらす concerns living one's life.\nDo not turn the second word into \"make it dark\": its meaning must be learned as a whole.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** follow the stacked shapes 艹, 日, 大, 日, as if a day were sinking toward\nthe bottom of the page. This is a modern memory aid, not a reconstruction of the character's origin.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe table selects the two native verbs; ボ remains in the full source metadata.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| く.れる | kun | 暮れる くれる — grow dark; come to an end |\n| く.らす | kun | [暮らす](../words/暮らす.md) くらす — live; lead a life |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [暮らす](../words/暮らす.md) くらす — live; get by\n- 暮れる くれる — grow dark; end, of a day or year\n- 暮らし くらし — day-to-day life; livelihood\n\n## Notes\n\nKeep the kana endings visible: 暮れる and 暮らす are different verbs.\n[春](春.md) and [早](早.md) also stack strokes around 日; [映](映.md) places 日 on the left.\nThese are modest shape comparisons, not close matches to every part of 暮.\n\nVocabulary: JMdict entries 1514940, 1514960 and 1514930.\n",
